{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     hero-variant — the post header's art direction, tag → class.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Emits ONLY the modifier class. It is a partial rather than an inline
     chain because the answer is needed in more than one place on the page —
     the header element and, for the full-bleed variants, the media slot — and
     a chain copied twice drifts the first time a sixth variant is added.

     `#hero-1` … `#hero-5` map onto NSDS's own `.ns-posthead` modifiers, so
     five header treatments cost this theme no CSS:

       1  (default)   left-aligned, cover below the standfirst
       2  --center    centred measure
       3  --wide      cover breaks out to the page container
       4  --split     text and cover side by side
       5  --bleed     full-bleed cover with the title over it

     Unrecognised or absent → the default. A post that predates the tag
     renders correctly rather than unstyled, which is the whole reason the
     `{{else}}` is empty rather than an error.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{~#has tag="#hero-2"~}} ns-posthead--center
{{~else has tag="#hero-3"~}} ns-posthead--wide
{{~else has tag="#hero-4"~}} ns-posthead--split
{{~else has tag="#hero-5"~}} ns-posthead--bleed
{{~/has~}}
